if there's one thing that's been clear  to me since I started playing the closed  beta for the crew it's that this is a  ubisoft game through and through it  takes place in a large and lavishly  produced world stuffed with things to do  it sends you from location to location  dizzying you with tasks that seem only  vaguely related to the goals of the  story this is entertainment for easily  distracted people like me the  distractions are built into the very  experienced the game itself distracting  me from itself with another way point  another goal another vehicle to drive  it's a formula that works but it's also  a formula that toes the line between  keeping you busy and making you feel  like you're just going through the  motions and based on the crew beta I'm  not sure that the game will land on the  proper side of that line but I can't  deny its appeal it all began from almost  the moment I signed into the game and  the initial chase sequence roared ahead  from there I've gone to Detroit to  Chicago to st. Louis to New York and  places in between chasing missions and  other tasks that earn me new Parts that  spruce up my two current vehicles of  ford mustang and the Ford Focus I also  are in perk points that I can spend on  upgrades that provide boosts like  experience bonuses I pursue the  waypoints I perform tasks like chasing  down rival gang members or rushing  someone to another section of the map  and I earn a reward it's you chasing and  it's compelling in that primal way that  games like diablo so often our ends like  in an action RPG i'm not necessarily  alone in the world i wouldn't call the  crew a massively multiplayer game but  you still share your gameplay session  with others and you can join up with  them to roam cities and the stretches in  between if you don't know way of these  folks and considering the crew uses you  play as its social portal you probably  won't  you can invite nearby players to join  you whenever you activate a mission  conversely you'll frequently receive  random requests to join others in their  own cooperative tasks afterwards you and  your crew can roam about together or you  can disband this structure means you can  easily hop from place to place provided  you've already driven once to the area  you're visiting occasionally I bounced  around from one city to another using  the quick travel system but I enjoyed  driving across the beautiful stretches  of Midwestern farms and towns even  though those expenses are far smaller  than their real life counterparts I mean  I drove from Chicago to New York in  about ten minutes after all in time  however the beta has proven somewhat  unsatisfying even after just a few hours  the never-ending quest for more powerful  cars aside there's not much to tie the  crew beta together I suppose the story  as Ubisoft's attempt to ground the crew  in a theme but at least in the beta it's  absolute nonsense full of ridiculous  dialogue and dumb story beats but  without the gung-ho silliness that could  have made it mindless fun as for the  driving I admit I'm spoiled by need for  speed rivals slick handling in the crew  beta of vehicles don't behave  consistently sometimes careening off of  the smallest objects as if they've  bounced from a trampoline making contact  with other vehicles doesn't always  result in the collision you expect but  rather might send you ricocheting away  as if the cars were covered with a thick  layer of rubber there's undoubtedly  plenty of time to tune up the physics of  horse but it was hard not to notice the  quirks in the crew beta the driving is  serviceable it's the sheer variety of  tasks and the constant call to group up  to go to a different city to do one of a  dozen available challenges that keeps  you on the move that said I'm really  looking forward to seeing how the crew  blossoms is the game nears its full  release this November it's a big n ultra  detailed game that in its current beta  state comes across as a bit random and  unfocused but a few major tune-ups could  make the crew an appealingly smooth ride  one that you could put a lot of miles on
 

